#!/bin/bash
# SessionStart hook (startup, resume, clear, compact): Claude sessions in the
# AmpUp workspace push and open PRs as ampup-bot, so I can approve them with
# my own account (git_approve_pr). Commits stay authored by me.
#
# Runs on every session start, so sessions brought back by a cmux restore get
# the same credentials as ones I launched by hand.
#
# - GH_TOKEN: gh and its git credential helper act as ampup-bot.
# - insteadOf: AmpUpTech SSH remotes go over HTTPS, so pushes use that
#   credential helper instead of my SSH key.

[ -n "$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE" ] || exit 0

cwd=$(jq -r '.cwd // empty')
case "$cwd/" in
  "$HOME/Workspaces/ampup/"*) ;;
  *) exit 0 ;;
esac

# Token lives only in 1Password; reading it asks for Touch ID.
token=$(op read --account ampup.1password.com 'op://Employee/gh_claude_pat/token' 2>/dev/null)
if [ -z "$token" ]; then
  echo '{"systemMessage":"claude-ampup-bot-env: could not read ampup-bot token from 1Password; git/gh will act as your account"}'
  exit 0
fi

{
  printf 'export GH_TOKEN=%q\n' "$token"
  echo "export GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1"
  echo "export GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0='url.https://github.com/AmpUpTech/.insteadOf'"
  echo "export GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0='git@github.com:AmpUpTech/'"
} >> "$CLAUDE_ENV_FILE"
